// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`notice templates > accounts-merged renders HTML and text without personal data 1`] = `
"Subject: Your Berth accounts were merged

Your accounts are now one

Two Berth accounts were merged into this one. Your orders, rewards and wallets are all here now.

Open Berth: https://www.berthmarkets.com/

This is a security notice. Berth sends these to every account with an email, whatever your email settings say.
Not you? Write to us at support@berthmarkets.com.

Berth. Wall Street, in your wallet."
`;

exports[`notice templates > assistant-connected renders HTML and text without personal data 1`] = `
"Subject: Claude was connected to your Berth account

An AI was connected

Claude was connected to your Berth account. It can:

* See what you own and your orders.
* Draft a buy or a sell, which you check and sign in Berth.

It cannot move your money or sign for you. You can disconnect it from your account at any time.

Open Berth: https://www.berthmarkets.com/

This is a security notice. Berth sends these to every account with an email, whatever your email settings say.
Not you? Write to us at support@berthmarkets.com.

Berth. Wall Street, in your wallet."
`;

exports[`notice templates > budget-low renders HTML and text without personal data 1`] = `
"Subject: Running low: the news model credit

A paid service is running low

The news model credit has $0.80 left, by Berth's own estimate.
At the last week's pace it runs out in about 4 days.

Top it up on the provider's own dashboard, then enter the new balance on the Budgets page. This email comes at most once a day for each service.

Open Budgets: https://www.berthmarkets.com/staff/budgets

You get this because you are a staff admin of Berth.
Not you? Write to us at support@berthmarkets.com.

Berth. Wall Street, in your wallet."
`;

exports[`notice templates > campaign-paid renders HTML and text without personal data 1`] = `
"Subject: $5 in USDC was added to your Berth account

Your offer was paid

$5 in USDC was sent to your Berth account on Base, for keeping your first buy through the offer.
It is yours to keep, spend or take out, like any other money in your wallet.

Open Berth: https://www.berthmarkets.com/

You get this because emails about your orders and payments are on.
Turn these off: https://www.berthmarkets.com/api/email/unsubscribe?t=sample-token

Berth. Wall Street, in your wallet."
`;

